    <compoundname>micro-test-plus-inits</compoundname>
    <title>Initialisation &amp; Exit</title>
    <sectiondef kind="func">
      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__micro-test-plus-inits_1gaa790667969dc1a261c324e89a6ea4591" prot="public" static="no" nodiscard="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::exit_code</definition>
        <argsstring>(void)</argsstring>
        <name>exit_code</name>
        <qualifiedname>micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::exit_code</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>void</type>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Complete the test run and return the exit code. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Parameters</title><para>None. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>0 if all tests were successful, 1 if any test failed.</para>
</simplesect>
In addition to the test cases defined in <computeroutput>main()</computeroutput>, additional test suites may be declared as static objects either within the same file or in other files, and are automatically registered via the static constructors mechanism.</para>
<para>The <computeroutput>exit_code</computeroutput> function finalises the execution of all registered test suites and test cases within the µTest++ framework, and returns an appropriate exit code to the operating system. This function should be called at the end of the test program, typically from the <computeroutput>main()</computeroutput> function, to ensure that all results are properly reported and the correct status is communicated.</para>
<para>The returned value indicates the overall success or failure of the test run, allowing integration with build systems and continuous integration environments. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
